## Phase 4: Portainer Administration & Architecture Templates

With your homelab successfully deployed, configure administrative access and expand your app template library [191, 192].

### Step 1: Initial Portainer Configuration
1. Open your web browser and navigate to the Portainer interface [191]:
   ```text
   http://<YOUR_PI_IP_ADDRESS>:9000
   ```
2. Create your administrative user account [191]. If you did not change default installer variables, use `admin` and the password specified under `AUTO_SETUP_GLOBAL_PASSWORD` in `dietpi.txt` [191, 641].
3. Under environments, select **Docker** and connect [191].

### Step 2: Inject Architecture-Optimized App Templates
Portainer's default list of application templates is basic [192]. To populate your homelab with dozens of optimized, ready-to-run server containers [172], swap the default settings with an architecture-specific template [175, 176]:

1. Click on **Settings** in the bottom-left corner of the Portainer sidebar [192].
2. Enable **Use external templates** [5].
3. Depending on your Pi's hardware, copy and paste the correct URL into the **App Templates** text field [175, 176]:
   * **ARM64 (64-Bit OS — Highly Recommended)** [175, 176]:
     ```text
     https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pi-hosted/pi-hosted/master/template/portainer-v3-arm64.json
     ```
   * **ARM32 (32-Bit OS — Legacy fallback only)** [175, 176]:
     ```text
     https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pi-hosted/pi-hosted/master/template/portainer-v2-arm32.json
     ```
4. Click **Save settings** [193].
5. Go to **App Templates** in the sidebar. You now have immediate access to 1-click deployments of the entire Pi-Hosted catalog [172, 175, 192]!

