## Phase 6: Customizing the Homer Portal & Quick Shortcuts

Access your new landing page at `http://<YOUR_PI_IP_ADDRESS>:8080` [165]. Because we bound the Homer container's path `/www/assets` to the persistent directory `/mnt/dietpi_userdata/homer/assets` on the host, you can easily tweak its YAML settings [165].

### Customize `config.yml` On The Fly
1. Open a terminal or use **File Browser** to navigate to `/mnt/dietpi_userdata/homer/assets/config.yml` [649].
2. Replace or edit the addresses with your exact host IP (e.g. replacing `localhost` with `192.168.0.x`).
3. Homer is static; as soon as you save the file, refresh your browser tab to see the updated page.

### Keyboard Shortcuts for Power Users [163]
Homer is optimized for speed and keyboard-first navigation. Try using these shortcuts directly on your landing page [163]:
* `/` — Immediately focuses the search bar and lets you start typing to filter your homelab applications [163].
* `Escape` — Stops your search, clears the query, and resets the interface [163].
* `Enter` — Opens the first matched result in your filtered list (conforming to your defined item's link target) [163].
* `Alt` (or `Option`) + `Enter` — Opens the first matched result in a brand-new browser tab [163].

